  "title": "Embeddings joined the API",
  "summary": "The API grew new capabilities while a week of compatibility fixes made the existing ones less surprising to use.\n\nAn OpenAI-compatible `/v1/embeddings` endpoint added a new way to turn content into vectors. It accepts batches of up to 32 text inputs and offers two OpenAI text models, with `openai-3-small` as the default. Paid-balance model `gemini-2` also accepts image, audio, and video content parts.\n\nLlama 4 Maverick and Scout added text-and-vision options with very large context windows; Maverick supports tools, while Scout does not. Paid-access Gemma 4 brought image input, tools, and reasoning. The `mistral` route moved to Mistral Small 3.1 after timeouts on its previous route, and existing 3.2 aliases now resolve to 3.1.\n\nPaid-only `seedance-2.0` added 4–15-second, 720p video from text, images, or reference frames, with optional native audio. Across the week, fixes addressed LTX-2 retrieval, Nova Reel generation, Nova Canvas requests, and self-hosted image dimensions. Video errors also became more specific, and Seedance 2.0 now validates aspect ratios before sending requests.\n\nPublishable App Keys no longer require a redirect URI. BYOP generation events can resolve an app’s name and owner from its key, and App Key owners can enable developer earnings with the share shown on consent screens. The dashboard separates App Keys from ordinary publishable keys, while app identification and redirect matching received fixes.",
